{% from "components/lead-form.njk" import leadForm with context %}
{% import "components/blocks.njk" as b with context %}
{% set tn = site.twoNumberPromise %}

<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="wrap--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">{{ tn.name }}</p>
    <h1>Two numbers, not one.</h1>
    <p class="lead mt-5">{{ tn.summary }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    <h2>Why anybody would do this</h2>
    <p>
      The loudest objection to selling a house for cash is that cash buyers lowball you.
      It is a fair objection. A cash offer <em>is</em> below retail, and most of the
      companies advertising for your house will not tell you when listing would net you more,
      because saying so costs them the deal.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are licensed, which means saying it does not cost us the deal. If the honest answer
      is "list it," we can be the ones who list it. That removes the reason to shade the
      truth, and it is the entire point of the promise.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--warm">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    <h2>How it actually works, in order</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>First, the cash offer &mdash; we are a buyer, not your agent</h3>
          <p>{{ tn.stage1 }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>With it, our honest read on what it would list for</h3>
          <p>
            What we think it realistically sells for on the open market, what it would cost
            you to get there, and what you would net after commission, closing costs, repairs
            and the months of carrying it. Compare the two <strong>net</strong> numbers, not
            the headline prices.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>Only if you'd rather list &mdash; a separate agreement</h3>
          <p>{{ tn.stage2 }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="promise promise--accent">
      <h3 class="promise__head">Why the order matters</h3>
      <p>
        We do not act as your agent and as the buyer at the same time. When we are buying,
        we are a principal spending our own money and we owe you no fiduciary duty &mdash;
        we tell you that plainly rather than let you assume otherwise. Only when you decline
        the cash offer and sign a listing agreement do we start working <em>for</em> you.
        The two never overlap, so you never have to wonder which side we are on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    <h2>When listing genuinely beats our cash offer</h2>
    <p>We will tell you to list when:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The house is in decent condition and a retail buyer could get a loan on it.</li>
      <li>You have two or three months and no hard deadline.</li>
      <li>You can live with showings and with a buyer's financing possibly falling through.</li>
      <li>The gap between our number and a realistic net listing is larger than the
      certainty is worth to you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>And we will tell you to take the cash offer when:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The house needs work a retail lender will not finance.</li>
      <li>You have a foreclosure date, a job start date, or a court date.</li>
      <li>It is inherited, full, and being managed from another state.</li>
      <li>There are tenants you would have to remove before you could list.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/compare/">See the full comparison, including iBuyers &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="wrap--narrow">
    <p class="small muted">
      {{ tn.disclosure }}{% if site.licenseNumber %} NC real estate license #{{ site.licenseNumber }}.{% endif %}
      Nothing on this page is legal, tax, or financial advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{ b.ctaBand("Get both numbers", "Start with the address. We'll come look at it, and you'll have the cash number and our read on the listing number in writing within " + site.offerWindowHours + " hours.") }}

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap--narrow">{{ leadForm("bottom-form", "full") }}</div>
</section>
